# =============================================================================
# Banglar Voice — Supabase project environment
# Copy to .env (root / frontend / mobile build machine) and fill real values
# from: Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API  (+ Edge Functions secrets)
# =============================================================================

# --- Public (safe to embed in Next.js / Flutter) -------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...your-anon-key...

# --- Server-only (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix NEVER used with these) -------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...your-service-role-key...
SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# --- Edge function secrets (Supabase > Edge Functions > Secrets) ---------------
# These are read by ai-process-report ONLY through the api_vault table —
# see README "API Vault" for the recommended pattern. Keep this block empty
# unless you choose to bypass the vault during early development.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=...
# ONESIGNAL_REST_KEY=...

# --- Outside Supabase (see README: what stays OUT) -------------------------------
# AI model access happens server-side in the vault; video transcoding & FCM
# delivery happen OUTSIDE Supabase. These vars live on Vercel / the worker:
# VERCEL_TOKEN=...
# ONESIGNAL_APP_ID=...
# MUX_TOKEN_ID=...
# MUX_TOKEN_SECRET=...
